  "body": "**The request (mkinney, 2026-11-15):** \"Do we need to handle svg file import?\" ... \"Yes file it\". Many waterjet, laser and plasma users draw in Inkscape or Illustrator and export SVG. WAZER's own app takes SVG and DXF (see #1525).\n\n## What\n\nImport an SVG file as 2D sketch geometry for 2D operations (Contour, Pocket, Engrave/Trace, plasma or waterjet profile). It goes into the same sketch entity as the DXF import, so the operations need no new input path.\n\n## Depends on\n\n- #1860 (DXF core reader), #1861 (2D sketch chaining, outer-vs-hole nesting, open chains) and #1862 (the sketch ECS entity, .camproj persistence, undoable import).\n- Stack on those: the SVG reader only produces sketch chains and reuses chaining, nesting and the import command.\n\n## Scope\n\n- **Elements:** `path` (M/L/H/V/C/S/Q/T/A/Z, absolute and relative), `line`, `polyline`, `polygon`, `rect` (with rx/ry), `circle`, `ellipse`. `g` groups with `transform` (matrix, translate, scale, rotate, skew), applied to the geometry.\n- **Curves:** cubic and quadratic Béziers and elliptical arcs become arcs or polylines within the document's chord tolerance. An arc stays an arc where it is circular after the transform.\n- **Units and scale:** `width`/`height` with units (mm, cm, in, pt, pc, px), and the `viewBox`. px uses 96 px/in (the CSS rule). If the file states no physical size, the import asks for the scale. It never guesses silently.\n- **Y axis:** SVG Y points down. Flip it so the drawing appears as it does in the editor.\n- **Ignored, with a note:** fill, stroke style, text (unless converted to paths), images, clip paths, masks, `use` references to symbols outside the file.\n- **Refusals, by name:** a malformed path, a zero or negative size, a degenerate arc, and a file larger than the import budget give a clear error, never a panic (the Prime Directive).\n- **MCP:** an `import_svg` tool, or the shared sketch-import tool with format svg (AGENTS.md \"Commands ship with an MCP tool\").\n\n## Not in scope (later)\n\n- Text to outlines (fonts), embedded images, and CSS stylesheets.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A fixture SVG set (a rectangle with a hole, Bézier and arc shapes, a nested group with transforms, mm and in documents, and one file without a physical size) imports to the expected sketch chains. The tests pin the chain count, closure, nesting and size within tolerance.\n- A 2D Contour on an imported SVG posts. A golden is pinned for one plasma or waterjet-style profile.\n- Malformed fixtures are refused by name and never panic. The importer fuzz test covers the SVG reader.\n- The user guide import page (and #1525's waterjet notes) lists SVG.\n\nRelated: #1525 (waterjet research), #1452 (DXF umbrella), #1860-#1870 (DXF chain).\n",
